"updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:21:09Z","body":"Hi @kradalby — thanks for the feedback. Understood on not wanting to expose internal cache state or take on extra registration-flow surface area.\r\n\r\nJust to clarify where I’m coming from: I don’t work on Clan, I’m only a user — but Clan’s networking abstraction is the real motivation behind this request. It’s a good example of an orchestration model that tries to make networking “just work” by integrating multiple network providers and driving them via external tooling/policy.\r\n\r\nIf you have a moment, this write-up gives the context better than I can paraphrase:\r\nhttps://clan.lol/blog/2025-wrap-up/\r\nhttps://docs.clan.lol/main/guides/networking/networking/\r\n\r\nI’m not attached to the exact mechanism I proposed here; the goal is simply to make it possible for an external controller/CLI to build a reliable approval UX around the existing interactive join behavior. If you have a preferred headscale-native solution (auth key workflow, hooks/events, etc.), I’d really appreciate your guidance and I can adjust or drop this PR accordingly.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3802218885/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"oneingan","id":810075,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDA3NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/810075?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneingan","html_url":"https://github.com/oneingan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneingan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneingan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneingan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneingan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onein